#: Game.Levels.Proposition.L01_MatchingGoals
msgid "Basic Propositions"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `a ≤ b`
#. §1: `∃ c, b = a + c`
#. §2: `a ≤ b`
#. §3: `c`
#. §4: `b = a + c`
#: Game.Levels.LessOrEqual.L01_LeRefl
msgid "§0 is *notation* for §1. This \"backwards E\"\n"
"means \"there exists\". So §2 means that there exists\n"
"a number §3 such that §4. This definition works\n"
"because there are no negative numbers in this game.\n"
"\n"
"To *prove* an \"exists\" statement, {pc: click | mobile: tap} the goal and build the\n"
"number that works. Let's see an example."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.LessOrEqual.L03_LeSuccSelf
msgid "If you build the wrong number, you get stuck with a goal you can't prove.\n"
"What number will you build here?"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `≤`
#. §1: `≠ 0`
#: Game.Levels.AdvMultiplication
msgid "In this world we prove how multiplication interacts with §0 and with §1: a factor of\n"
"a nonzero number is at most that number, a product is zero only if a factor is, and a\n"
"nonzero factor can be cancelled."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `le_refl x`
#. §1: `x ≤ x`
#. §2: $\\le$
#: Game.Levels.LessOrEqual.L01_LeRefl
msgid "§0 is a proof of §1.\n"
"\n"
"The reason for the name is that this lemma is \"reflexivity of §2\""
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.LessOrEqual.L09_LeOne
msgid "If you solved this level then you are ready for the boss!"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `a + b = 0`
#. §1: `a = 0`
#. §2: `≤`
#: Game.Levels.AdvAddition
msgid "In this world we prove some basic facts about addition that involve implications:\n"
"cancellation, and that §0 forces §1. These are the facts that §2 World\n"
"is built on."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `mul_comm x y : x * y = y * x`
#. §1: `mul_zero`
#. §2: `zero_mul`
#: Game.Levels.Multiplication.L02_ZeroMul
msgid "Our first challenge is §0,\n"
"and we want to prove it by induction. The zero\n"
"case will need §1 (which we have)\n"
"and §2 (which we don't), so let's\n"
"start with this."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `b ≠ 0`
#. §1: `b = 0 → False`
#. §2: `b = 0`
#. §3: `h`
#. §4: `False`
#: Game.Levels.AdvMultiplication.L02_MulLeftNeZero
msgid "Remember that §0 is §1: {pc: click | mobile: tap} the goal to assume §2,\n"
"then §3 is a short way to §4."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Rewrite
msgid "Rewrite World"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Multiplication.L09_MulAssoc
msgid "We now have enough to prove that multiplication is associative,\n"
"the boss level of multiplication world. Good luck!"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `≤`
#. §1: `a + b = 0`
#. §2: `a = 0`
#. §3: `b = 0`
#. §4: `a`
#. §5: `b`
#. §6: `cases`
#. §7: `cases`
#. §8: `b = 0`
#. §9: `b = S d`
#. §10: `hd`
#. §11: `b`
#. §12: `cases`
#. §13: `b`
#. §14: `b = 0`
#. §15: `b = S d`
#: Game.Levels.AdvAddition.L05_AddRightEqZero
msgid "The next result we'll need in §0 World is that if §1 then §2 and §3.\n"
"Let's prove the first of these facts in this level. The second follows from it by\n"
"swapping §4 and §5, so you'll get that one for free.\n"
"\n"
"## A new tactic: §6\n"
"\n"
"The §7 tactic will split an object or hypothesis up into the possible ways\n"
"that it could have been created.\n"
"\n"
"For example, sometimes you want to deal with the two cases §8 and §9 separately,\n"
"but don't need the inductive hypothesis §10 that comes with induction on §11.\n"
"In this situation you can drag §12 onto §13 instead. There are two ways to make\n"
"a number: it's either zero or a successor. So you will end up with two goals, one\n"
"with §14 and one with §15."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `a ≠ 0`
#. §1: `b ≠ 0`
#. §2: `a * b ≠ 0`
#. §3: `a`
#. §4: `b`
#. §5: `S`
#. §6: `a * b`
#. §7: `S`
#. §8: `zero_ne_succ`
#: Game.Levels.AdvMultiplication.L07_MulNeZero
msgid "This level proves that if §0 and §1 then §2. One strategy\n"
"is to write both §3 and §4 as §5 of something, deduce that §6 is\n"
"also §7 of something, and then use §8."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `add_sq a b`
#. §1: $(a+b)^2=a^2+b^2+2ab.$
#: Game.Levels.Power.L09_AddSq
msgid "§0 is the statement that §1"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `t = 0`
#: Game.Levels.AdvMultiplication.L01_MulLeMulRight
msgid "Let's warm up with an easy one, which works even if §0."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `a ≠ 0`
#: Game.Levels.AdvMultiplication.L03_EqSuccOfNeZero
msgid "Multiplication usually makes a number bigger, but multiplication by zero can make\n"
"it smaller. Thus many lemmas about inequalities and multiplication need the\n"
"hypothesis §0. Here is a key lemma that enables us to use this hypothesis."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.PropositionRight.L03_IffOr
msgid "If and Only If (Disjunctions)"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `add_right_cancel a b n`
#. §1: $a+n=b+n\\implies a=b$
#: Game.Levels.AdvAddition.L01_AddRightCancel
msgid "In this world I will mostly leave you on your own.\n"
"\n"
"§0 is the theorem that §1."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.LessOrEqual.L03_LeSuccSelf
msgid "Successor is Increasing"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Power.L06_PowAdd
msgid "Let's now begin our approach to the final boss,\n"
"by proving some more subtle facts about powers."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `succ_le_succ x y`
#. §1: `S x ≤ S y`
#. §2: `x ≤ y`
#: Game.Levels.LessOrEqual.L08_SuccLeSucc
msgid "§0 is a proof that if §1 then §2."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `b`
#: Game.Levels.AdvMultiplication.L09_MulRightEqSelf
msgid "The lemma proved in this level will be helpful in Divisibility World, one day.\n"
"Splitting §0 into its two forms does most of the work."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Neq
#: Game.Levels.NeqJoined
msgid "Equalities are propositions too. Prove some, and prove that some numbers are different."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `ℕ`
#: Game.Levels.LessOrEqual.L10_LeTotal
msgid "Very well done.\n"
"\n"
"A passing mathematician remarks that you've just proved that §0 is totally\n"
"ordered."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `add_comm`
#. §1: `succ_add`
#. §2: `succ_add a b`
#. §3: `(S a) + b = S (a + b)`
#. §4: `a`
#. §5: `b`
#. §6: `x + y = y + x`
#. §7: `b`
#. §8: `b = 0`
#. §9: `b`
#: Game.Levels.Induction.L02_SuccAdd
msgid "Oh no! On the way to §0, a wild §1 appears. §2\n"
"is the proof that §3 for §4 and §5 numbers.\n"
"This result is what's standing in the way of §6. Again\n"
"we have the problem that we are adding §7 to things, so we need\n"
"to use induction to split into the cases where §8 and §9 is a successor."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.PropositionBonus.L01_AllTogether
msgid "Many Such Cases"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `a ^ b`
#. §1: `pow_zero a : a ^ 0 = 1`
#. §2: `pow_succ a b : a ^ S b = a ^ b * a`
#. §3: `add_sq`
#. §4: $(a + b)^2$
#: Game.Levels.Power
msgid "In this world we define powers, §0, by two more axioms: §1\n"
"and §2. Everything else about powers follows from\n"
"these, by induction. The boss of this world is §3, the formula for §4."
msgstr ""

#: Game
msgid "Natural Numbers Video Game"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Induction
msgid "Induction World"
msgstr ""

#. §0: $x,y,z>0$
#. §1: $m \\geq 3$
#. §2: $x^m+y^m\\not =z^m$
#. §3: $m \\geq 3$
#. §4: `n + 3`
#. §5: `m`
#. §6: `x > 0`
#. §7: `a + 1`
#: Game.Levels.PowerBonus.L01_FLT
msgid "We now have enough to state a mathematically accurate, but slightly\n"
"clunky, version of Fermat's Last Theorem.\n"
"\n"
"Fermat's Last Theorem states that if §0 and §1 then §2.\n"
"If you didn't do inequality world yet then we can't talk about §3,\n"
"so we have to resort to the hack of using §4 for §5,\n"
"which guarantees it's big enough. Similarly instead of §6 we\n"
"use §7.\n"
"\n"
"This level looks superficially like other levels we have seen,\n"
"but the shortest solution known to humans would translate into\n"
"many millions of lines of Lean code. The author of this game,\n"
"Kevin Buzzard, is working on translating the proof by Wiles\n"
"and Taylor into Lean, although this task will take many years.\n"
"\n"
"## CONGRATULATIONS!\n"
"\n"
"You've finished the main quest of the natural number game!\n"
"If you would like to learn more about how to use Lean to\n"
"prove theorems in mathematics, then take a look\n"
"at [Mathematics In Lean](https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathematics_in_lean/),\n"
"an interactive textbook which you can read in your browser,\n"
"and which explains how to work with many more mathematical concepts in Lean."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.Outro.L01_ThankYou
#: Game.Levels.Outro
msgid "The End"
msgstr ""

